                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_12\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit modifies the single-selection branch inside SavedHqlExportToCSV.export()\n(the \"else\" branch handling options that do NOT allow multi-selection, e.g. SUBJECT or\nDEPARTMENT). Before the fix, the code unconditionally did:\n\n    String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());\n    SavedHQLInterface.IdValue v = new SavedHQLInterface.IdValue();\n    v.setValue(option.name());\n    Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);\n    if (id == null) {\n        try { id = Long.valueOf(value); } catch (NumberFormatException e) {}\n    }\n    v.setText(id == null ? \"\" : id.toString());\n    params.add(v);\n\nThe bug: when `value` is null (the parameter was not actually supplied for this request,\ne.g. because it's a single-choice HQL report parameter without a selection), the code\nstill built and added an IdValue with an empty/garbage text and no valid id, which broke\nCSV export for reports containing a single-choice parameter. The fix wraps this whole\nblock in `if (value != null) { ... }` so no parameter entry is created when the value is\nabsent.\n\nTracing the history of this file across candidates:\n- candidate_12's diff shows this exact block being added as brand-new code (`+` lines),\n  including the single-selection \"else\" branch with `helper.getParameter(option.name())`\n  followed immediately by unconditional IdValue creation/lookup/add \u2014 with no null check\n  on `value`. This is the very first appearance of the buggy pattern.\n- candidate_13's diff touches the same file (hash 035a4b20d..2f093afe5) but only adds a\n  new SavedHQLParameter loop after this block; it does not modify or fix the\n  single-selection branch, so the bug persists unchanged.\n- candidate_14's diff is byte-for-byte identical to fix_commit_diff.txt (same blob hashes\n  2f093afe5..857ee9502), meaning candidate_14 is actually the fix commit itself, not a\n  bug-introducing candidate.\n\nSince candidate_12 is the first commit to introduce the unguarded single-selection value\nhandling that the fix later corrects with the `if (value != null)` check, it is the\nbug-introducing commit.\n"
